Why this approach: dependencies must be decided before any task imports them; versions were looked up with go list -m outside the repo so go.mod stays unchanged until T3 and T10.
Alternatives rejected: ncruces/go-sqlite3 (own Go VFS, not SQLite's), mattn/go-sqlite3, DataDog/zstd, valyala/gozstd, google/brotli bindings (all cgo); Postgres, MongoDB; masking or encrypting body secrets in v1.
Trade-off / known limit: raw request storage grows quadratically with session length; klauspost/compress's module also carries Apache-2.0 (gzhttp) and MIT (s2 filepathx) code, not imported; zstd is BSD-3-Clause.
Verified by: make verify; go.mod and go.sum unchanged; licences read from the module cache (modernc.org/sqlite v1.59.0, klauspost/compress v1.20.1, andybalholm/brotli v1.2.5).
